-- title:
--   §5, unnumbered: unit resource cone and its three inequalities
-- statement:
--   Let $U\subseteq\mathbb R^3$ be the cone generated by the entanglement-distribution, superdense-coding and teleportation rate vectors $(0,-1,1)$, $(2,-1,-1)$, and $(-2,1,-1)$, respectively. For every real triple $(C,Q,E)$,
--
--   $$ (C,Q,E)\in U\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad C+2Q\le0,\qquad Q+E\le0,\qquad C+Q+E\le0.$$
--
--   Membership on the left means a linear combination of the three displayed vectors with nonnegative real coefficients. This is the algebraic characterization of the source-defined unit-resource cone.
-- source:
--   The quantum dynamic capacity formula of a quantum channel, arXiv:1004.0458v3, PDF p. 7, §5, unnumbered: unit resource cone and its three inequalities

